# Dev broker ACL: the rules a production broker gets for homescope (see
# docs/design/deployment-topology.md, "Topics and ACL on the central broker"),
# with the site `dev` standing in for a real one. Keeping them identical is the
# point: a topic that drifts from these rules fails here, in dev, as an API
# that receives nothing, instead of first failing on a production broker that
# does not log ACL denials.
#
# No rule = no access. Mosquitto reloads this file only on restart or SIGHUP.

user homescope-api
topic read homescope/+/sensors/+/envelope

user homescope-dev
topic write homescope/dev/#
